# REST API for Book Management — Verbose Educational Example

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional RESTful API for managing a collection of books using **Node.js** and **Express.js**. The API follows standard HTTP conventions (GET for reading, POST for creating, PUT for full updates, DELETE for removal) and uses an in-memory array as its data store. Every function is documented with JSDoc, every route includes inline curl examples, and custom error classes ensure consistent error responses across all endpoints.

---

## File 1: `package.json`

```json
{
  "name": "book-rest-api",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "A simple REST API for managing books using Node.js and Express.js",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "dev": "nodemon server.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "nodemon": "^3.0.1"
  }
}
```

> **Why this structure?** `package.json` declares our dependencies and scripts. We use `express` for the HTTP framework and `nodemon` in development so the server auto-restarts on file changes. The `"main"` field points to our entry point, `server.js`.

