# 📚 Book REST API

A simple, educational REST API for managing books built with Node.js and Express.js.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+ 
- npm (comes with Node.js)

## Installation

```bash
npm install
```

## Running the Server

```bash
# Production mode
npm start

# Development mode (auto-restarts on file changes)
npm run dev
```

The server starts on `http://localhost:3000` by default. Override with `PORT=8080 npm start`.

## API Endpoints

### GET /books — List All Books

Returns all books, optionally filtered by query parameters.

```bash
# Get all books
curl http://localhost:3000/books

# Filter by genre
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?genre=Fiction"

# Filter by author (substring match)
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?author=hawking"

# Filter by year range
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?yearFrom=1950&yearTo=2000"
```

