# Books REST API

A simple, educational REST API for managing books built with Node.js and Express.js. This project demonstrates core API design patterns including CRUD operations, error handling, middleware, and in-memory data storage.

## Features

- **Full CRUD** — Create, Read, Update, and Delete books
- **Filtering** — Filter books by genre, author, year, or search term
- **Statistics** — Aggregate stats including counts by genre and decade
- **Error Handling** — Custom error classes with consistent JSON error responses
- **Validation** — Input validation with meaningful error messages

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+ installed
- npm (comes with Node.js)

## Installation & Setup

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <repository-url>
cd books-rest-api

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start the development server (with auto-reload)
npm run dev

# Or start the production server
npm start
```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:3000`.

## API Endpoints

### Books

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/books` | List all books (with optional filters) |
| GET | `/books/:id` | Get a single book by ID |
| POST | `/books` | Create a new book |
| PUT | `/books/:id` | Update an existing book |
| DELETE | `/books/:id` | Delete a book |

### Statistics

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/stats` | Get aggregate statistics |

## Testing the API

### Using curl

```bash
# 1. Check that the server is running
curl http://localhost:3000/

# 2. List all books (initially empty)
curl http://localhost:3000/books

# 3. Create a new book
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"The Hobbit","author":"J.R.R. Tolkien","genre":"Fantasy","publishedYear":1937}'

# 4. Create another book
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Dune","author":"Frank Herbert","genre":"Science Fiction","publishedYear":1965}'

# 5. List all books
curl http://localhost:3000/books

# 6. Get a single book by ID
curl http://localhost:3000/books/1

# 7. Update a book
curl -X PUT http://localhost:3000/books/1 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"The Hobbit - Special Edition"}'

# 8. Filter books by genre
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?genre=fantasy"

# 9. Search books
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?search=tolkien"

# 10. Delete a book
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/2

# 11. Get statistics
curl http://localhost:3000/stats
```

