## Resumo das Escolhas de Design

| Decisão | Justificativa |
|---------|--------------|
| Array em memória | Simples, didático, preserva ordem de inserção |
| `express.Router()` | Modularidade e reutilização de rotas |
| Classes de erro customizadas | Diferenciação clara de tipos de erro (404 vs 400 vs 409) |
| Validação antes do store | Fail-fast — evita operações desnecessárias com dados inválidos |
| Partial update no PUT | Mais flexível para o consumidor da API |
| Resposta padronizada `{success, data}` | Consistência que facilita o consumo pela frontend |
| Middleware de erro por último | Requisito do Express para识别 correto como handler de erro |
| Health check na raiz | Facilita testes de conectividade e descoberta de endpoints |

# 📚 Book Management REST API — Educational Implementation

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional **RESTful API** for managing books using **Node.js + Express.js**. It follows industry-standard conventions (HTTP methods, status codes, JSON payloads) and is structured to be both production-ready in concept and deeply educational. Every function, route, middleware layer, and design decision is documented with JSDoc comments and inline explanations so you can understand not just *how* the code works, but *why* each pattern was chosen.

The API uses **in-memory storage** (an array) for simplicity — no database setup required — making it ideal for learning REST principles, middleware composition, error handling strategies, and request/response lifecycle in Express. It includes filtering on list endpoints, comprehensive validation, custom error classes, statistics aggregation, and a complete README with curl/Postman examples.

