# REST API for Book Management — Educational Implementation

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional RESTful API using **Node.js** and **Express.js** that manages a collection of books in memory. The design follows modern best practices: separate concerns across multiple files, comprehensive JSDoc documentation, custom error classes with middleware, input validation, query-based filtering, and aggregate statistics. Every function is explained so learners can understand *why* each pattern was chosen — from REST conventions (proper HTTP verbs and status codes) to async/await for readable asynchronous flow, from in-memory storage (simple, no external dependencies) to structured error handling (consistent client feedback). The API supports the full CRUD lifecycle plus a stats endpoint, making it an ideal teaching tool for anyone learning backend development with Express.

